      "summary": {
        "nb": "Kampen kirke er soknekirke for Kampen menighet i Oslo domprosti i Oslo bispedømme i bydel Gamle Oslo i Oslo kommune. Den er en treskipet langkirke og ble ble innviet 29. november 1882. Kirken het fra først av Betlehems kirke, men navnet festet seg aldri og gikk snart ut av bruk.",
        "en": "Kampen Church is a church in Oslo, Norway, in the Kampen area. On 29 November 1882, the church was consecrated. Following a fire in Kampen in 1878, a new church became part of the neighborhood's restoration plans. A new congregation was established in the neighborhood in 1880, but it gathered elsewhere until the church finished its construction."
